{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "fierymud_legacy/src: cleric.cpp, sorcerer.cpp, sorcerer.hpp, rogue.cpp, rogue.hpp, warrior.cpp, mobact.cpp (mob_attack class switch, check_mob_status), ai_utils.cpp (mob_heal_up)",
  "notes": [
    "Rules are per FAMILY; 'classes' maps Class.plain_name to the families it runs, in order. Hybrids run cleric rules first, then warrior rules (mob_attack falls through), so the warrior family uses priority 500+.",
    "Each rule names an Ability.plain_name. The seeder only creates a ClassAiRules row when the class has that ability in ClassAbilities (spells, songs, chants) or ClassSkills (skills; its min_level becomes ClassAiRules.min_level).",
    "priority is legacy array order (lower first). chance_pct is 0-100. conditions use the mob_ai_rules.rs JSON keys only. target is one of auto, self, tank, weakest_attacker, caster, most_buffed, lowest_ally, room.",
    "align applies to the TARGET's alignment band (as target_lifeforce does). Alignment of the caster itself is not expressible.",
    "Engine contract: skip a buff the mob already has and a hindrance the target already has; apply the 'best 2-3 attempts' cap; legacy 'victim level < mob level + 20' for hindrances.",
    "chance_pct for warrior/rogue/bard is a static approximation of legacy 'level% per round' at a level-50 mob; ClassAiRules has no level-scaled chance.",
    "'legacy' on a rule is documentation only and is not written to the database."
  ],
  "gaps": {
    "race_rules": "dragonlike_attack (breath / sweep / roar for dragon, dragonborn and demon races) is race-driven; ClassAiRules is keyed by class only. Needs a RaceAiRules table or per-proto MobAbilities. See race_rules_legacy.",
    "conditions_missing": [
      "target_hp_above (sorcerer buffs/harness/poison need victim HP > 15/75/80)",
      "self alignment and negated target alignment (flamestrike, divine ray, stygian eruption, hell bolt, divine bolt, holy/unholy word caster side)",
      "negated lifeforce (degeneration, soul tap, energy drain skip undead/magic)",
      "target level < mob level + 20",
      "equipment (shield, piercing weapon)",
      "room (outdoors for earthquake)",
      "which debuff the mob has (cure rules)"
    ],
    "chance": "no level-scaled chance; legacy warrior/rogue/bard 'level% per round' approximated statically"
  },
  "race_rules_legacy": {
    "chance": "roll = rand(0, 150 - level); breath if roll < 5, sweep if roll < 10, roar if roll < 15 (about 10% each at level 100)",
